\section{Integral-State Regularization Analysis}
\label{sec:integral-regularization-theory}

The $\vct S=\vct 0$ pseudo-measurement is part of the core estimator, not part
of the sea-state tuner.  It is also deliberately false for real wave motion:
$\vct S$ is generally nonzero.  Its role is therefore best understood as a
regularizer whose Kalman gain suppresses low-frequency integration drift while
inevitably rejecting some desired low-frequency motion.  This section analyzes
that mechanism with reduced linear models before any particular adaptation law
is introduced.

